    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0317" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg245"/>

                <head>No. 8.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Earl Granville to Sir E.
                    Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 1,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have now to notify to you the
                    transmission, on the 28th ultimo, to its destination of the communication which,
                    as I informed you in my dispatch of the 24th ultimo, I was about to address to
                    Mr. Lowell relative to the arrests, under the peace preservation (Ireland) act
                    of 1881, of Joseph B. Walsh and Daniel Sweeney, or McSweeney.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
